  "content": {
    "id": "p6-q28-response",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "",
    "prompt": "A plane flies at a constant elevation of $200\\text{ m}$. Initially, the plane is directly above an observer. Five seconds later, the angle of depression of the observer from the plane is $5^\\circ$. How fast is the plane moving? Express your answer in metres per second. Give your answer correct to two decimal places.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": {
        "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "p6-q28-short-result",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "\\frac{40}{\\tan5^\\circ}\\text{ m/s}\\approx457.20\\text{ m/s}",
                "display": false
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p6-q28-short-method",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Use tangent to find the horizontal distance travelled, then divide by 5 seconds.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Let $x$ metres be the horizontal distance travelled in $5$ seconds and $v$ be the speed in metres per second. The angle of elevation at the observer equals the $5^\\circ$ angle of depression because the horizontals are parallel.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\tan5^\\circ&=\\frac{200}{x}\\\\x&=\\frac{200}{\\tan5^\\circ}\\\\v&=\\frac{x}{5}\\\\v&=\\frac{200}{5\\tan5^\\circ}\\\\v&=\\frac{40}{\\tan5^\\circ}\\\\v&\\approx457.20\\end{align*}$$\nThe speed is $457.20\\text{ m/s}$, correct to two decimal places.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 76
  },
